==================== Input ====================
# Bail-out 1, at the two edges a block mapping's span does not cover.
#
# A block mapping has no closing token, so `mapping.span` stops at its last entry. Both a
# same-line trailing comment and a deeper-indented end-comment run sit past that point and
# are still claimed by the mapping's printing, so the refusal scope reaches past the span.
openapi: 3.0.0
paths:
  /trailing:
    get:
      responses: {}
      operationId: op # trailing comment past the span end
  /end-comments:
    get:
      responses: {}
      operationId: op
        # deeper-indented end comment, also past the span end

